Subject: [PATCH] ACPI: use noncoherent SROOT DMA when NVDA8600 omits _CCA

NVIDIA N1X BIOSes may omit ROT0._CCA while their IORT routes the
NVDA8600 revision-1 SROOT device through SMMUv3 with noncoherent
memory properties. The Windows nvsrootmbx provider explicitly
requests MmNonCached memory for its bounded DMA common buffer.

Treat only this missing-attribute case on NVDA8600 (_HRV == 1) as
noncoherent before normal platform DMA configuration. Preserve
explicit/inherited attributes and other revisions/devices. Do not
borrow DLA0's coherent DMA device or bypass the firmware-declared
IOMMU route.

---
diff --git a/drivers/acpi/scan.c b/drivers/acpi/scan.c
--- a/drivers/acpi/scan.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/scan.c
@@ -1707,7 +1707,25 @@
 					       NULL, &cca);
 		if (ACPI_SUCCESS(status))
 			adev->flags.cca_seen = 1;
-		else if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ACPI_CCA_REQUIRED))
+		else if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ACPI_CCA_REQUIRED) &&
+			 status == AE_NOT_FOUND &&
+			 !strcmp(acpi_device_hid(adev), "NVDA8600")) {
+			unsigned long long revision;
+
+			/* N1X BIOSes may omit ROT0._CCA despite its IORT DMA mapping.
+			 * IORT declares noncoherent memory through SMMUv3. The Windows
+			 * SROOT provider requests an explicitly noncached common buffer.
+			 * Keep the normal ACPI/IORT DMA path and architecture cache
+			 * maintenance; do not borrow DLA0's coherent DMA device/domain.
+			 */
+			if (ACPI_SUCCESS(acpi_evaluate_integer(adev->handle,
+						 "_HRV", NULL, &revision)) &&
+			    revision == 1) {
+				adev->flags.cca_seen = 1;
+				acpi_handle_info(adev->handle,
+					"NVDA8600 SROOT: using noncoherent DMA for missing _CCA\n");
+			}
+		} else if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ACPI_CCA_REQUIRED))
 			/*
 			 * If architecture does not specify that _CCA is
 			 * required for DMA-able devices (e.g. x86),
